-- title:
--   The adic completion of a Noetherian local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative ring that is Noetherian and local, with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_O$, and let $\widehat O =$ `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal O) O` be its $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion, regarded as an $O$-algebra via `algebraMap`. The assertion is the existence of an instance witnessing that $\widehat O$ is a local ring and an instance witnessing that the structure map $O \to \widehat O$ is a local homomorphism (the preimage of the non-units is contained in the non-units), together with three further statements about the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_{\widehat O}$ determined by that local ring structure: first, $\widehat O$ is $\mathfrak m_{\widehat O}$-adically complete (`IsAdicComplete`, i.e. the $\mathfrak m_{\widehat O}$-adic filtration is Hausdorff and every Cauchy sequence for it converges); second, the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_O$ in $\widehat O$, namely $\mathrm{Ideal.map}$ of $\mathfrak m_O$ along $O \to \widehat O$, equals $\mathfrak m_{\widehat O}$; and third, every $x \in \widehat O$ differs from the image of some $o \in O$ by an element of $\mathfrak m_{\widehat O}$, so that $O/\mathfrak m_O \to \widehat O/\mathfrak m_{\widehat O}$ is surjective. The residue-field statement is given in this surjectivity form rather than as an isomorphism of fields.
--
--   This is the standard package of facts about the completion of a Noetherian local ring: the completion is local and complete, $\mathfrak m_O \widehat O = \mathfrak m_{\widehat O}$, and the residue field is unchanged. It serves as the basic input for the work with complete local rings in the deformation-theoretic part of the argument, and is used in the analysis of étale and power-series presentations of completions and of their residue fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_isLocalRing_adicCompletion_isAdicComplete_map_maximalIdeal_eq.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
